  "scope": "Strict bounded portable template bundles retain full definitions and referenced assistant profiles without source IDs or credentials. Native selected/all JSON/gzip export, content-detected input, inert complete preview, cancel/Escape, private-field rejection, actual EIO preservation/retry, fresh shared assistant/template IDs, same-name originals, unbound templates, complete gzip backup and normal restart are verified with zero model requests. An actual Escape focus failure is preserved and fixed by an explicit import opener reference. Six complete-run captures are individually reviewed at light 1280×840 and dark 760×540 100/125/150 percent. Final type/build, 660 tests and all 215 desktop checks pass; the bundle contract and template service have complete coverage. Three new release-policy tests reject prior 210-check bodies and absent, partial, requesting or nonboolean transfer evidence. Draft content/context are exact; ordinary autosave timestamp/undefined-property normalization is excluded from object comparisons, while the actual EIO primary-file hash is exact. Picker and confirmation responses are isolated native fixtures; physical picker, foreign formats and wider platform checks remain open. Historical 210-check installer evidence keeps its old application hashes and cannot satisfy the new minimum 215 release gate."
